    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHey, after ff68fd6b8a I started getting `return _statusline_component(...)73314B written` instead of the usual `<file> written` in excmd messages.\n\nI debugged a bit and found this line https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/ff68fd6b8a84ce83c14358db1d70a562f1524ebe/src/nvim/lua/executor.c#L1599\n\nAfter `redrawstatus` gets executed, the IOBuf is dirty and gets written out in subsequent `nvim_echo`  somewhere after this point https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/ff68fd6b8a84ce83c14358db1d70a562f1524ebe/src/nvim/bufwrite.c#L1710\n\nThis happens when you have such an autocmd in your config:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"Progress\" }, {\n    callback = function()\n        -- vim.schedule(function() [DOES NOT HAPPEN WITH VIM.SCHEDULE]\n        vim.cmd(\"redrawstatus!\")\n        -- end)\n    end,\n})\n```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\nedit randomfile\nsource 👇 \n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"Progress\" }, {\n    callback = function()\n        -- vim.schedule(function()\n        vim.cmd(\"redrawstatus!\")\n        -- end)\n    end,\n})\n```\n\n\nwrite\n\nObserve: `local _A=select(1,...) return ((packag...' ') or '' ).progress_status()) or '' )` instead of `<file> written`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNormal file written message like always.\n\nThis patch fixes the problem it:\n\n```patch\ndiff --git a/src/nvim/lua/executor.c b/src/nvim/lua/executor.c\nindex 1771a01565..decd309f55 100644\n--- a/src/nvim/lua/executor.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/lua/executor.c\n@@ -1593,10 +1593,11 @@ void nlua_call_typval(const char *str, size_t len, typval_T *const args, int arg\n {\n #define CALLHEADER \"return \"\n #define CALLSUFFIX \"(...)\"\n+  static char buf_iosize[IOSIZE];\n   const size_t lcmd_len = sizeof(CALLHEADER) - 1 + len + sizeof(CALLSUFFIX) - 1;\n   char *lcmd;\n   if (lcmd_len < IOSIZE) {\n-    lcmd = IObuff;\n+    lcmd = buf_iosize;\n   } else {\n     lcmd = xmalloc(lcmd_len);\n   }\n@@ -1609,7 +1610,7 @@ void nlua_call_typval(const char *str, size_t len, typval_T *const args, int arg\n \n   nlua_typval_exec(lcmd, lcmd_len, \"v:lua\", args, argcount, false, ret_tv);\n \n-  if (lcmd != IObuff) {\n+  if (lcmd != buf_iosize) {\n     xfree(lcmd);\n   }\n }\n```\n\nIf this is the correct place to fix this, then I'l gladly open a PR.\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-c4af59647f\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nlinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ntmux\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n-\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source",
